  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 430 AM EDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nHeading into Friday, the upper high slides west towards Texas as its \nnegatively tilted upper ridge rotates east through the northern \nPlains. Northwest flow, ahead of the ridge, will push a surface high \nthrough eastern Canada as a the cold front south of the high drops \nsouth interacting with shortwaves riding around the upper high, near \nthe CWA. This is expected to increase shower and thunderstorm \nchances that are expected to work their way south through the CWA. \nNot expecting much in the way of total rainfall, but additional \ncloud cover and a shift to northerly winds could help bring relief \nfrom warm temperatures. The timing looks delayed, so at least parts \nof the Heat Advisory may need to be extended into Friday.  \n\nSaturday, the front is expected to begin moving back north as a warm \nfront. WAA will keep high temperatures in the low to mid 90s through \nthe beginning of next week before widespread 80s return. The overall \npattern remains a little messy with a general zonal flow over the \nLower Ohio Valley. A surface low/frontal system is expected to bring \nincreased shower and thunderstorms chances for the beginning and \nmiddle parts of next week. Overall rainfall amounts remain low.",
